Return exactly the lowercase word sufficient only if the reports cover the requested material claims with precise primary-source URLs and concrete supporting findings from sources the researcher says it actually retrieved. Check that source findings support the claims, required source counts and dates are covered, limitations are explicit, and lab results are distinguished from field results. A bibliography, plausible prose, metadata, search snippets, an app availability/quota error or an unsupported assertion of success is not sufficient. Research requests to resolve conflicting studies or provide independent corroboration need that evidence too. Respect the requested scope: do not invent extra research requirements.

